<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hungarian Revolution of 1956</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1956">1956</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Hungarian Uprising</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hungarian Revolution of 1956 was a countrywide revolt against the government of the Hungarian People's Republic and its subordination to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>. It began in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/budapest">Budapest</a> on 23 October 1956, when students marched to the Parliament and ÁVH police fired on protesters at the radio building; militias and workers' councils then took control in many places. The new government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imre-nagy">Imre Nagy</a> disbanded the ÁVH, declared <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>'s withdrawal from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw-pact">Warsaw Pact</a> on 1 November and pledged free elections. Soviet troops moved in on 4 November and crushed the uprising; about 2,000 Hungarians and 700 Soviet soldiers were killed, and some 200,000 Hungarians fled abroad, mostly to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>Hungarian Revolution of 1956</b> was crushed by more than 150,000 Soviet troops; nearly 20,000 Hungarians died and Imre Nagy was hanged in 1958.</blockquote><a href="/empire/hungary">Hungary · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
